{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "washtenaw-county-hotelling",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.41, step 7f: the SINGLE-county input database of `process-extended-idle-single`, `process-apu-single` and `process-crankcase-extidle-single`, as the onroad chain mounts it. Like `inputs/washtenaw-project.esm` it is the scale-input-database half of a run's catalogue: it declares the run's DOMAIN and the domain-owned tables and mounts `onroad/default-database.esm` for the rest.\n\nWHAT THE DATABASE IS. moves.rs builds `washtenaw_cdb` in MariaDB from `characterization/county-inputs/washtenaw-county/setup-hotelling.sql` and captures only the execution database MOVES merges it into. The SQL states rows for seven tables by literal INSERT -- `state`, `county`, `zone`, `zoneRoadType`, `roadTypeDistribution` (source type 62), `year`, `sourceTypeYear` -- and two hotelling tables, `hotellingHoursPerDay` (2 rows) and `hotellingActivityDistribution` (12 rows, zone 261610, diesel); creates `hotellingHourFraction`, `hotellingAgeFraction` and `hotellingMonthAdjust` EMPTY; and copies `sourceTypeAgeDistribution`, `HPMSVtypeYear` and `fuelSupply` from the default database by `INSERT ... SELECT`, because MOVES does not copy those three from the default at SINGLE scale (InputDataManager.java:1435, :2834-2846). tools/build-scale-input-db.py writes the stated and the empty tables to `inputs/washtenaw-county-hotelling/`, typed by the default database's schemas, with the RunSpec's SINGLE.\n\nTHE MERGE, TABLE BY TABLE, each measured against the default database at the run's keys (PLAN.md §7.3.41):\n\n* `zoneRoadType` -- a ROW MERGE whose input rows DIFFER: the four allocation factors are the default's truncated to twelve decimal places, up to 5.75e-10 relative, and the execution database holds the truncated ones. Declared here as `db_input_zoneroadtype`; the model writes the precedence (`zrt_mergedSHOAllocFactor`).\n* `hotellingActivityDistribution` -- a ROW MERGE whose input rows ADD keys: zone 261610's twelve rows beside the default's 36 at 990000. Declared here as `db_input_hotellingactivitydistribution`; the model writes the precedence (`had_isMerged`) and MOVES's choice of zone (`hot_activityZoneID`, 261610 here). It is not the default's distribution: the county states 3% shore power for model years 2010 and later where the default states none, and no CNG row at all.\n* `hotellingHoursPerDay` -- a row merge whose default side is EMPTY, so it is this table: declared whole.\n* `hotellingHourFraction`, `hotellingAgeFraction`, `hotellingMonthAdjust` -- empty on both sides, declared so that `run_domainUnported` would count a row.\n* `state`, `county`, `roadTypeDistribution`, `year`, `sourceTypeYear` -- row merges over the default's own rows, IDENTICAL at every value (measured, 0 relative), read from the default database by the joins that already select them (docs/esm-conventions.md 92).\n* `zone` -- truncated like `zoneRoadType`, but no hotelling calculation reads it.\n* `sourceTypeAgeDistribution`, `HPMSVtypeYear`, `fuelSupply` -- REPLACED at SINGLE scale, by copies of the default's rows at the run's year and fuel region; identical at every key the model reads, so read from the default database, as `washtenaw-project` reads its `fuelSupply` and `IMCoverage`. `IMCoverage` is replaced by nothing (the county database has none), and the default's has no row for county 26161 in any year.\n* `link` and `linkSourceTypeHour` -- not domain-specific at SINGLE scale: MOVES copies the default's national `Link` into every domain but PROJECT, so this document declares the default's, as `moves-onroad.esm` does.\n\nIT DOES NOT LOAD ALONE, like `moves-onroad.esm`: it names no runspec.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "onroad",
      "domain",
      "single-county-domain",
      "scale-input-database"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_link": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/Link.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_link"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "output",
          "domain"
        ],
        "note": "Link, the default database's national table: MOVES merges it into every domain but PROJECT (InputDataManager.java:1432), so a SINGLE-county run reads the same 22,610 synthetic links a DEFAULT one does, and selects county 26161's on-network and off-network ones by its joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_linksourcetypehour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/linkSourceTypeHour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_linksourcetypehour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "linkSourceTypeHour, the default database's: 0 rows, and the county database has none. Only ProjectTAG reads it.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecdomain": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-county-hotelling/runspecdomain.parquet"
